---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About" compact>
  <article class="wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>About Kaletopia</h1>
      <p>
        Kaletopia is an art project for humanity. It is a curated encyclopedia of history and ideas
        where an entry can be read as text, imagery, video, or an interactive simulation, on any device.
        Some entries are two paragraphs and a photograph. Some let you turn the dials on a model
        and watch what happens.
      </p>
      <p>
        It starts with the subjects its editor cares about and grows from there. It is not for
        profit and never will be. The writing is licensed CC BY-SA 4.0, the same license Wikipedia
        uses, and the code is MIT. Both live in the open on
        <a href="https://github.com/lucaspfeiffer/kaletopia">GitHub</a>, where anyone may propose an
        entry or improve one.
      </p>
      <h2>Why</h2>
      <p>
        A good explanation of how something happened is rarer than a record that it happened.
        Simulations let a reader ask "what if" of history and of ideas, and that is a kind of
        understanding a paragraph cannot give. Kaletopia is a place to collect those explanations
        and keep them working.
      </p>
      <h2>Contributing</h2>
      <p>
        Read <a href="https://github.com/lucaspfeiffer/kaletopia/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">the contributing guide</a>
        and open a pull request. Entries are edited, and the bar is craft, not coverage.
      </p>
      <h2>Editor</h2>
      <p>Lucas Pfeiffer. Kaletopia began as a newsletter at <a href="https://www.kaletopia.com">kaletopia.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
<style>
  article { padding-top: 2rem; }
  h1 { font-size: 2.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
</style>
